The short answer: to make it nudgeable.

The long answer:

Well, that acid blob more or less kicked off the
mess.

See, I'd left my pet bat behind on the level below
Sokoban (it being pretty useless to try to herd a
bat to the stairs), and so I entered Sokoban
petless.

I was pushing the third from last boulder north on
the first Sokoban level, and when I got back to the
south horizontal leg, there was an acid blob in my
way, and no pet to kill it for me. I didn't want the
experience points, early loss of my original pet had
me up to experience level 6 already. so, rather than
kill the acid blob, rather than wait forever for it
to back out of my way, only, probably, to trap me
again for each subsequent boulder, i charmed it. Now
the "kick pet" patch that has become a part of
vanilla NetHack let me move it out of my way by
bumping into it. Once the silliness had begun, I
just decided to see how much more silly I could make
it.

I managed to herd the whole menagerie up to
top-level Sokoban, adding a couple of more or less
useful psts (two cats), and several useless ones
along the way.  Major lesson learned: if you are
going to make a pet out of a nymph, WAKE HER UP
FIRST! Even if you bump her out of the way, she
doesn't wake up, and it was just too unfair to peg a
gem at her to awaken her, so she sat like a stump
at the last spot to which i displaced her.

In the end, as always, now experience level 7 due to
several other mishaps, I panicked. Having filled in
all the holes on the top level, and turned the
corner to the south passage down to the zoo door, I
let a bunch of large ants panic me, ran out of Pw
and HP, forgetting completely the wand of lightning
I was carrying that would have fried them quickly,
and died. Turned out my unIDed sack was a bag of
holding, just brim full of spellbooks and scrolls
some unlucky shopkeeper had donated earlier, too.

That wasn't as bad, though, as a game earlier today
where I starved to death on top level Sokoban, which
had no scrap of food for me, and despite that I was,
it turned out, carrying an unIDed ring of slow
digestion. I'd angered my god a while back by too
early a desperate food prayer, and found no altar to
mollify him, but scratched successfully through five
or so levels anyay. That ironic kind of ending just
makes me foam at the mouth, and want to scratch fleas
and bark at the moon.

xanthian.

